{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 3, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Hark to thee knight of wanderlust who dost seek the fair lands of Nihon where cherry blossoms do kiss the breeze and lanterns glow like stars upon earth. Behold thy seven-day sojourn crafted in rhyme most grand where every hour shall take thee by the hand.\n\n**Upon the First Day of Thy Quixotic Quest**\nAwake thou at the break of dawn and don thy finest garb for Tokyo’s embrace is fierce yet fair. To Shibuya’s heart thou shalt repair where neon lights do dance and crowds like waves ebb and flow. At Hachiko’s statue stand thou still and pay heed to love’s unyielding might. Then to Meiji Shrine forthwith where ancient gods do dwell and trees stand tall as sentinels of time. Feast thy flesh at Ichiran Ramen where humble bowls of fire shall warm thy soul.\n\n**Second Day Brings Thee to the East**\nDepart thou for Asakusa where temples stand in golden light. Sensoji’s bell shall ring out clear a call both sweet and old. Wander through Nakamise’s stalls where trinkets gleam and treasures bold await thy hand. A cruise on Sumida’s river shall reveal the skyline fair a sight to stir the heart’s desire.\n\n**Upon the Third Day Mount Fuji’s Shadow Doth Call**\nTo Hakone thou must away where hot springs bubble and steam does rise to kiss the sky. Upon a ropeway ascend high where views unfold of Fuji’s crown so bright. Stroll through hells of old where souls do walk in wooden guise and stories dark and twisty rise.\n\n**Fourth Day Sees Thee Ride the Bullet’s Might**\nBoard the train swift as a comet’s flight to Kyoto where temples rest beneath the moon’s soft light. Fushimi Inari’s torii gates shall march in endless array like soldiers standing guard through day and night. At Gion’s quarter loiter soft where geisha glide like ghosts of yore and teahouses whisper secrets of old lore.\n\n**Fifth Day Whispers of History’s Breath**\nTo Nara thou must now repair where deer do roam with gentle grace and feed on sacred crackers thrown by thy hand. Todai-ji’s Buddha doth sit vast and wise with eyes that hold the cosmos in their gaze. Return thou to Kyoto for Arashiyama’s bamboo grove where stalks do sway like dancers in a mystical groove.\n\n**Sixth Day Brings Visions of the Sea**\nTo Hiroshima’s shores thou travelest where peace doth bloom amidst the ruins left behind. The dome stands stark yet serene a monument to hope reborn. To Miyajima’s island sail where its floating torii gate doth beckon thee to tread upon the waters fair.\n\n**Seventh Day Crowns Thy Journey’s End**\nTo Osaka thou dost turn for one last feast most grand. At Dotonbori’s heart the food is bold bright lights and laughter fill the air. Behold the castle plum and towering signs that speak of dreams both wild and free. With full heart and stomach heavy leave thou Japan’s fair shores thy soul forever changed by lands where ancient meets the new in perfect harmony.", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.16029712557792664}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.003225721186026931}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -2.9867587089538574}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0396350733935833}, {"token": "e", "logprob": -0.0018114125123247504}, {"token": " knight", "logprob": -8.248381614685059}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.18303421139717102}, {"token": " wander", "logprob": -1.6072418689727783}, {"token": "lust", "logprob": -0.02414814941585064}, {"token": " who", "logprob": -2.233731985092163}, {"token": " dost", "logprob": -0.49505147337913513}, {"token": " seek", "logprob": -0.5750296711921692}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.9865594506263733}, {"token": " fair", "logprob": -0.9706665277481079}, {"token": " lands", "logprob": -2.149160146713257}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.038732945919036865}, {"token": " N", "logprob": -2.497307300567627}, {"token": "ih", "logprob": -0.06206206604838371}, {"token": "on", "logprob": -0.0013502062065526843}, {"token": " where",